course: dictionary
lesson: 9049
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. «I'm a light sleeper, so the slightest noise wakes me.» Here a sleeper is a person who wakes up easily, because the words light and wakes are the clues.
explain: «Rails are fixed to sleepers laid on a bed of stones.» Now sleeper means something quite different. Rails and stones are the clues, so this sleeper is a heavy beam under a railway track, not a person at all. Always ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look for the clue words. A sleeper train, a rough sleeper and a heavy sleeper all use the same word, but each one is a different meaning. Use the words around the word to decide which meaning is right.
fact: A sleeper can be a person or animal who is asleep, such as a light sleeper or a heavy sleeper.
fact: A light sleeper wakes up easily; a heavy sleeper is hard to wake up.
fact: A sleeper train has beds for passengers to sleep in during a long journey.
fact: In the UK and Australia, a sleeper is a heavy wooden or concrete beam under the railway tracks. In the US, it is called a tie.
fact: «Rough sleeper» means a homeless person who sleeps outside.
exercise: «I'm a light sleeper, so the slightest noise wakes me.» What does light sleeper mean? | Someone who never goes to bed | Someone who sleeps on a train | Someone who snores very loudly | *Someone who wakes up easily
exercise: «Rails are fixed to sleepers laid on a bed of stones.» In this sentence, what is a sleeper? | A bed on a train | *A heavy beam under the railway tracks | A person who is asleep | A small earring
exercise: Dad says, «We're catching the sleeper to Scotland tonight.» What is the sleeper? | *A train with beds | A wooden beam under the rails | A person who snores | A bed in a garden
test: Some gardens have raised beds made from old railway sleepers. What are railway sleepers used for in this sentence? | To make earrings | *To make raised beds | To make sleeper trains | To hold up a tent
test: «He is a heavy sleeper, and his alarm clock rarely wakes him.» What does heavy sleeper mean? | Someone who sleeps only in the day | *Someone who is hard to wake up | Someone who weighs a lot | Someone who is always cold
exam: «When a whale sinks, crabs, hagfish and sleeper sharks eat the meat.» In this sentence, what is a sleeper shark? | A person who sleeps at sea | A type of train | *A type of shark | A type of whale
